From 663ad36baaf4b5c0d23f41ffb2d4c02d05db72cb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gus Bourg <gus@bourg.net>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 09:14:36 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 119/210] media: amlogic: add the video decoder core

Add the meson-amvdec platform driver to replace staging meson/vdec on
GXBB, GXL, GXLX, GXM, G12A, G12B and SM1. Provide a stateless-only V4L2
request interface with mem2mem scheduling, control snapshots, timestamp
reference lookup and explicit input and capture-buffer ownership.

Control the VDEC_1 and VDEC_HEVC blocks, their clocks, microcode and
parser input. Retain the microcode DMA source for the device lifetime
and quiesce decoder DDR requests before releasing buffers. Provide
canvas mapping, DMA guards and request watchdog/event-recording helpers.
The dma_guards parameter enables allocation guards; job_watch_ms sets
the request timeout, with zero disabling it.

Per-compatible codec descriptors carry coded-size, bit-depth, profile
and level limits and generate the profile/level menus. Each compatible
has its own format table; G12B reuses the G12A compatible. HEVC supports
Main and Main10 at 3840x2160 on every SoC. VP9 supports profiles 0 and 2
at that size on GXL, GXM, G12A, G12B and SM1. GXBB and GXLX have no VP9.
H.264 retains its 1920x1088 limit on GX and 3840x2160 on G12/SM1;
MPEG-2 is limited to 1920x1088 everywhere.

CAPTURE uses NV12M, with decoder double-write producing 8-bit output
for 10-bit input. G12/SM1 additionally support AM21C compressed scatter
capture. Native compressed GX export is outside this series.

Parser DMA uses a per-device completion initialized before each fetch
with a bounded, non-interruptible 200 ms wait.

Firmware paths are under meson/vdec/. GXBB/GXL/GXLX use
gxl_h264_multi.bin, gxl_hevc.bin and gxl_mpeg12_multi.bin; GXM uses
gxm_h264_multi.bin for H.264. GXL/GXM add gxl_vp9.bin.
G12A/G12B use g12a_h264_multi.bin,
g12a_hevc_mmu.bin and g12a_vp9.bin. SM1 uses sm1_h264_multi.bin,
sm1_hevc_mmu.bin and sm1_vp9_mmu.bin. All families use
gxl_mpeg12_multi.bin for MPEG-2. The *_multi images are not yet in
linux-firmware.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5.5 Claude:claude-fable-5.1 Codex:gpt-5.6 Codex:gpt-6.0
[chewitt: set allow_cache_hints on the CAPTURE queue so userspace can
 request non-coherent buffers for CPU readers such as software
 deinterlacing, which takes 1080i MPEG-2 read-back on GXM from 35 to
 90 fps]
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Signed-off-by: Christian Hewitt <christianshewitt@gmail.com>
